# Astro components

Write each `.astro` file in this order:

1. Frontmatter: imports, a short `Props` interface, plain prop names, a few lines of logic.
2. HTML: semantic tags (`section`, `h1`–`h3`, `ul`, `a`, `dl`).
3. One `<style>` block for classes used only in this file.

```astro
---
interface Props {
  title: string;
  summary: string;
  year: number;
}
const { title, summary, year } = Astro.props;
---

<article class="project-card">
  <h2 class="project-card__title">{title}</h2>
</article>

<style>
  .project-card__title { font-size: var(--type-title); }
</style>
```

- One block name per component: `hero`, `project-card`, `case`.
- Pages assemble components; they do not hold an entire screen in one file.
- When the same HTML chunk appears in two files, extract a component.
- Use `<script>` or `client:*` only when HTML and CSS cannot do the job.
